---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Convocados"
  description="The terms that apply when you use Convocados on the web, the Android apps, or through an AI assistant connected over MCP."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective 2 November 2026</p>

    <p>
      Convocados is a game-organising app run by José Cabeda ("we", "us"). These terms
      cover the website at <code>https://convocados.cabeda.dev</code>, the Android apps,
      and the MCP server at <code>https://convocados.cabeda.dev/api/mcp</code>. By using
      them you agree to these terms. How we handle personal data is described in the
      <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You need an account to create or join games. Give accurate details, keep your
      credentials to yourself, and tell us if you think someone else has used your
      account. You must be at least 16 years old. You are responsible for what happens
      through your account, including actions an AI assistant takes with a token you
      approved.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not use Convocados to break the law, harass people, or post content you have
        no right to share.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to access accounts, games or data you were not invited to, or to
        bypass rate limits, authentication or authorisation.</li>
      <li>Do not overload the service: no scraping, no automated bulk calls outside the
        published API and MCP tools, and no reselling access.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may suspend or close an account that breaks these rules.</p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep ownership of what you put into Convocados — game details, rosters, scores,
      messages. You give us permission to store and show it to the people who can see the
      game, which is what the app is for. Games, rosters, scores and ratings belong to the
      group you played with: deleting your account detaches your entries but does not
      erase the group's history, as described in the privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Costs and payments</h2>
    <p>
      Convocados is free to use. When an organiser records what a player owes for a court
      or a ball, that is a record between the people in the group: Convocados does not
      process the payment, hold the money, or guarantee that anyone pays. Settle up
      between yourselves.
    </p>

    <h2>AI assistants</h2>
    <p>
      You can connect an AI assistant (for example Claude or ChatGPT) over MCP. The
      assistant acts with the permissions you approve on the consent screen, and write
      actions only work for games you own or administer. Your use of the assistant is also
      governed by that provider's terms; we are not responsible for what it does with what
      you ask it.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>
      The service is offered as it is. We aim to keep it running and your data safe, but we
      do not promise uninterrupted availability, and features may change or be removed. If
      we make a material change to these terms we update this page and the date at the top;
      continuing to use Convocados after that means you accept the new terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending your use</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using Convocados at any time. To delete your account, sign in on the web
      at <a href="https://convocados.cabeda.dev">convocados.cabeda.dev</a>, open your profile
      and choose <strong>Delete account</strong> — the steps are in
      <a href="/docs/delete-account">the deletion guide</a>. If you cannot sign in, write to
      <a href="mailto:cabeda@proton.me">cabeda@proton.me</a> and we will delete it for you. We
      may suspend or end access if these terms are broken, or if the service is discontinued.
      Provisions that by their nature survive — content ownership, disclaimers, liability —
      survive.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimers and liability</h2>
    <p>
      Convocados helps a group organise a game; it does not run the game, the venue or the
      payments. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or
      consequential losses, or for losses caused by an assistant acting on your
      instructions. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have as a consumer under the
      law that applies to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the law of Portugal, without affecting the consumer
      protections of the country where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:cabeda@proton.me">cabeda@proton.me</a>,
      or open an issue in the
      <a href="https://github.com/Cabeda/Convocados/issues">public issue tracker</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 32px 20px 64px;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color-scheme: light dark;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 32px 0 8px;
  }
  .legal .updated {
    opacity: 0.65;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .legal li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
  .legal code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .legal {
      color: #e6e6e6;
    }
    .legal a {
      color: #7fc7a4;
    }
  }
</style>
